    "Several days of progressively worsening bilateral leg swelling and severe pain in chronic lower extremity wounds.",
    "Patient reported red to purple discoloration, wound drainage, peeling skin, generalized fatigue, and subjective fever.",
    "Vitals were afebrile at 36.1 C, HR 73/min, RR 17/min, BP 104/72 mmHg, and oxygen saturation 100%.",
    "Exam showed diffuse erythema with violaceous/dusky discoloration, marked edema, epidermal sloughing, necrotic tissue, hemorrhagic bullae, black eschars, and diffuse tenderness without crepitus.",
